course: dictionary
lesson: 147
title: Words of warmth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Affectionate means showing love and fondness in a gentle way, such as with hugs, kind words or cuddles. You can tell a word is about feelings when the sentence shows someone being caring or close to another person or pet.
explain: Read this from a famous story: «a soft-hearted and affectionate fellow, very easily converted». Soft-hearted means kind and tender, so affectionate must describe a warm, loving character. The words around it are the clues.
explain: Try the swap test. Put a simple meaning in place of the hard word: «a soft-hearted and loving fellow» still makes sense, so you have found the meaning. Affectionate is also used in phrases like «affectionate hug» and «affectionate nickname».
fact: Affectionate means showing love and fondness in a gentle way.
fact: «Affectionately» is the adverb: it tells you how something is done, in a loving way.
fact: An affectionate pet likes to be stroked and stay close to people.
fact: «Affectionately known as» means a person is called a name that shows love, such as a nickname.
fact: Adding an ending like -ka to a name can make it sound affectionate, as in the pet forms Solomiyka and OlEnka.
exercise: «a soft-hearted and affectionate fellow» What does affectionate mean here? | Tired and sleepy | *Loving and warm-hearted | Angry and rude | Very quick at running
exercise: The Rat says Toad is «so simple, so good-natured, and so affectionate». What kind of friend is Toad? | Loud and bossy | Tall and thin | Cold and far away | *Kind and loving
exercise: Solomiyka and OlEnka are pet forms of girls' names. What does the ending -ka do? | *It makes the name sound loving and friendly | It makes the name longer and harder to say | It makes the name a boy's name | It turns the name into a place
test: Mia gave her puppy a soft, affectionate cuddle. How is the puppy most likely to feel? | *Loved and happy | Hungry for dinner | Scared of the dark | Bored of walks
test: Which word means in a loving, gentle way? | Angrily | *Fondly | Quickly | Loudly
exam: Which word is the adverb form of affectionate? | affectionate | *affectionately | afflict | affection
